From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:01 2001
From: vamos <vamos@comma.ai>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 19:00:00 -0700
Subject: ufs: qcom: disable low-power capabilities (gating, scaling, power collapse)

Boot-time and idle UIC storms (pwr ctrl / uic cmd completion timeouts,
TSTBUS dumps, degraded link) on the comma four, even with phy_calibrate()
on resume (patch 0019) and clock gating alone removed (v1 of this patch):
gear changes from clock scaling still stormed. Remove all the UFS
low-power windows for bring-up.
---

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
index eba0e6617..75aa3aa41 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -1159,12 +1159,15 @@ static void ufs_qcom_set_host_caps(struct ufs_hba *hba)
 
 static void ufs_qcom_set_caps(struct ufs_hba *hba)
 {
-	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_CLK_GATING | UFSHCD_CAP_HIBERN8_WITH_CLK_GATING;
-	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_CLK_SCALING | UFSHCD_CAP_WB_WITH_CLK_SCALING;
+	/*
+	 * comma four (SDM845): clock gating, hibern8-with-clk-gating, clock
+	 * scaling (gear-change pwr ctrl), and aggressive power collapse all
+	 * contribute to a boot-time/idle UIC storm (pwr ctrl / uic cmd
+	 * completion timeouts, link left degraded), even with phy_calibrate()
+	 * on resume. Disable the low-power windows entirely for bring-up.
+	 */
 	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_AUTO_BKOPS_SUSPEND;
 	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_WB_EN;
-	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_AGGR_POWER_COLLAPSE;
-	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_RPM_AUTOSUSPEND;
 
 	ufs_qcom_set_host_caps(hba);
 }
